---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How We Work — Engagement Models"
  description="Choose how you work with us — a dedicated FTE, flexible pay-as-you-go support, or full portfolio management — built around your practice's workload."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Module of Work</p>
      <h1>Choose the Way You Want to Work With Us</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Every practice is different, so once we understand how you work, we'll help you pick the
        model that fits — or mix and match as your needs change.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid--3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>1. FTE Module</h3>
          <p>A dedicated team member (or team) who works exclusively on your practice, following your hours and your systems — like an in-house hire, without the recruitment, training, or overhead.</p>
          <p><strong>Best suited to:</strong> firms with a steady, ongoing volume of work who want consistent, dedicated capacity.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>2. Pay As You Go</h3>
          <p>Only pay for the work you send us, when you send it — no minimum commitment and no idle capacity.</p>
          <p><strong>Best suited to:</strong> firms with fluctuating workloads, seasonal peaks, or overflow work, or anyone who'd like to test the relationship before committing further.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>3. Portfolio Management Services</h3>
          <p>Hand over full ownership of a client portfolio — bookkeeping, accounts, tax, and everything in between — and we manage it end-to-end under your brand, reporting back on whatever schedule suits you.</p>
          <p><strong>Best suited to:</strong> firms looking to free up significant capacity by outsourcing entire client relationships, not just individual tasks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Not Sure Which Fits?</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        That's exactly what the introductory call is for — we'll talk it through and recommend a
        starting point, with plenty of room to adjust as we go.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact">Book a Free Consultation</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
